WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.540
Modelling instruction basically kind of turns
things upside down in the way that science

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.000
is approached in the high school classroom.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.460
Students are now presented at the beginning
of the unit with basically a lab experience.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:18.680
Can tables two through five — two through
five — go to one of the tutorials?

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:19.720
One of the four tutorials.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.990
They’re presented with some sort of a system
they can develop questions about themselves

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.519
and design experiments to assess these questions.

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:34.250
The data they collect we can then use to create
models that represent not only the system

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:39.310
but then can be generalized to represent any
system that shares these specific characteristics.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:44.210
The idea is that the students are really constructing
their own understanding through engaging in

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.210
this work.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.100
And the work tends to be a little more genuine
and authentic.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:54.000
As opposed to doing a lab for which theoretically
we should already know the outcome for and

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.820
we’re just going to calculate a percent
error for.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.710
So they’re actually engaging in work that
scientists are actually engaging in, constructing

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:02.210
models.

